(:adr
  :id "D83"
  :shortcode "D83"
  :title "RPC-First Record Store, Attention Separation, and Event-Driven Memory Architecture"
  :status :active
  :planStatus :approved
  :date "2026-09-13"
  :cluster "architecture/memory"
  :deciders ["user" "architect" "planner" "implementer" "auditor"]
  :problem "Autonomous agents currently write directly to filesystem files in .asl/mem/ (tasks, decisions, notes, receipts, telemetry, plans, phases, components, intents, principles, recipes). This direct-write model creates severe cognitive attention dispersal: agents must simultaneously formulate semantic goals and micro-manage low-level S-expression formatting, delimiter balance, and string escaping. Furthermore, concurrent subagent writes to shared files cause race conditions and syntax corruption, and direct file coupling prevents remote integrations (Jira, GitHub) and live agentic observability without polling disk."
  :drivers [
    "Attention Separation: Agents emit strictly pure semantic forms to asl rpc; the native engine guarantees 100% balanced delimiters, canonical formatting, and zero comments."
    "Cognitive Typestate Hierarchy: Cluster records into Tier Alpha (frictionless <80 tokens: notes, receipts, telemetry), Tier Beta (normative: decisions, intents, principles, recipes, components), and Tier Gamma (execution DAG: tasks, phases, plans)."
    "Bounded Blamed Rejection: Write-time schema validation returns concise error receipts (<80 tokens) naming the exact violated field, completely preventing agent context blowout."
    "Deterministic Persistence: Native C storage engine with flock file locking and atomic rename eliminates concurrent write collisions across parallel subagents."
    "Event-Driven Observability: Mutations emit structured events on an observability bus, powering live dashboards and remote integrations without disk polling."
    "Step-Scoped Context Delivery: Agents retrieve only the exact step-scoped context and active leases needed via (:where), eliminating monolithic file reads."
  ]
  :evidence [
    ".asl/mem/notes.asn is 120KB and .asl/mem/receipts.asn is 94KB, causing high context load when parsed."
    "Concurrent subagents appending to notes.asn frequently produce unbalanced S-expressions failing Gate 2."
    "Post-factum validation in asl audit consistency discovers schema errors only after file writes, causing expensive recovery loops."
    "ADR D58 mandates externalized deliberation and compact ASN protocols to preserve attention reliability."
    "ADR D59 mandates typestate decomposition and tiered memory hierarchy to eliminate cognitive sprawl."
  ]
  :decision "Adopt the RPC-First Record Store and Event-Driven Memory Architecture as ADR-0083 (D83). Mandate that all monorepo records (tasks, decisions, receipts, plans, phases, telemetry, components, intents, notes, principles, recipes) transition from direct filesystem writes to native RPC operations via asl rpc. Enforce write-time schema validation in asl/tools/asl.c, deterministic VFS persistence with atomic flock and rename, and structured mutation event streaming."
  :invariants ["C1" "C2" "C3" "C4" "C5" "D34" "D51" "D52" "D58" "D59" "D81" "D83"]
  :tasks [
    "Task48401"
    "Task48402"
    "Task48403"
    "Task48404"
    "Task48405"
    "Task48406"
    "Task48407"
    "Task48408"
  ]
  :settledChoices [
    (:choice :id mutationInterface :value "Pure ASN batch forms to asl rpc instead of direct filesystem writes")
    (:choice :id validationTiming :value "Synchronous write-time schema validation in native C engine before persistence")
    (:choice :id rejectionFormat :value "Bounded blamed receipts under 80 tokens specifying :field, :expected, and :hint")
    (:choice :id concurrencyLocking :value "Native flock with 2000ms bounded timeout and atomic temporary-file rename")
    (:choice :id storageAbstraction :value "Pluggable StorageEngine C interface defaulting to VFS adapter with SQLite and remote adapters enabled")
    (:choice :id observabilityHook :value "Structured mutation event emission on stdout and unix socket stream for zero-polling listeners")
  ]
  :outcomes [
    "Eliminates syntax and delimiter corruption in memory files by delegating serialization to C engine"
    "Shields agent attention window from filesystem mechanics and formatting micro-management"
    "Prevents context blowout on validation errors through compact blamed receipts"
    "Enables safe concurrent execution of parallel subagents via atomic file locking"
    "Provides unified event stream for agentic observability, live dashboards, and Jira/GitHub sync"
  ]
  :consequences [
    (:pos "Dramatically improves agent attention focus and execution reliability")
    (:pos "Guarantees 100% delimiter balance and comment-free purity across all memory files")
    (:pos "Eliminates race conditions and clobbered records in multi-agent swarms")
    (:pos "Enables seamless plugging of remote databases or mesh stores without changing agent tools")
    (:neg "Requires implementing comprehensive schema validators and storage adapters in asl.c")
    (:neg "Requires migrating existing direct-write scripts and updating agent prompt rules")
  ])
